=== tickets.Service.find
kind: def
src: internal/tickets/tickets.go :: func (s *Service) find(
doc: Finds a ticket the caller may see. Every action on a ticket starts here, so a ticket someone may not see looks to them like one that does not exist.
---
def find(actor, id):
    ticket = tickets[id]
    if none or not CanView(actor, ticket):
        raise TicketNotFound
    return ticket

=== tickets.Service.Open
kind: def
src: internal/tickets/tickets.go :: func (s *Service) Open(
doc: Starts a ticket for a customer, routes it to a team by its topic, starts its deadline and tells the team.
---
def Open(actor, input):
    #> Work out who the ticket is for -> accounts.Directory.Customer | CustomerNotFound
    customer_id = actor.CustomerID
    if actor.IsAgent():
        customer_id = input.customer_id
    customer = accounts.Directory.Customer(customer_id)
    #> A subject and a message are needed | MissingText
    if subject or body is empty:
        raise MissingText
    #> Read the priority -> deadlines.ParsePriority | UnknownPriority
    priority = ParsePriority(input.priority)
    #> A customer's plan caps the priority -> deadlines.HighestFor | PriorityNotAllowed
    highest = deadlines.HighestFor(customer.Plan)
    if actor.IsCustomer() and priority is above highest:
        raise PriorityNotAllowed
    #> Route it to a team by topic -> accounts.Directory.TeamForTopic
    team = accounts.Directory.TeamForTopic(input.topic)
    #> Create the ticket, with the message as its first reply
    ticket = Ticket(customer, team, priority, Status="new")
    add Reply(body, by actor)
    #> Start the deadline -> tickets.Service.startClock
    startClock(ticket)
    #> Tell the team -> tickets.Service.announceOpened
    announceOpened(ticket, by=actor)
    return visibleTo(actor, ticket)

=== tickets.Service.Get
kind: def
src: internal/tickets/tickets.go :: func (s *Service) Get(
doc: Returns one ticket with the replies the caller may read.
---
def Get(actor, id):
    #> Find a ticket they may see -> tickets.Service.find | TicketNotFound
    ticket = find(actor, id)
    #> Leave out what they may not read -> tickets.visibleTo
    return visibleTo(actor, ticket)

=== tickets.Service.List
kind: def
src: internal/tickets/tickets.go :: func (s *Service) List(
doc: Lists the tickets a person may see, optionally of one status. The ones with the nearest deadline come first.
---
def List(actor, status=None):
    #> Keep the tickets they may see -> tickets.CanView
    list = tickets where CanView(actor, ticket)
        and (no status asked or ticket.Status == status)
    #> Leave out what they may not read -> tickets.visibleTo
    list = visibleTo(actor, each)
    #> Most pressing first
    sort list:
        tickets with a deadline first, soonest DueAt on top
        then the rest, newest OpenedAt first
    return list

=== tickets.Service.Reply
kind: def
src: internal/tickets/tickets.go :: func (s *Service) Reply(
doc: Adds a message to a ticket. A customer's reply brings the ticket back to us, an agent's answer ends the customer's wait, and an agent's internal note changes nothing.
---
def Reply(actor, id, body, internal):
    #> Find a ticket they may see -> tickets.Service.find | TicketNotFound
    ticket = find(actor, id)
    #> A message is needed | MissingText
    if body is empty:
        raise MissingText
    #> A customer's reply brings the ticket back to us -> tickets.Service.customerReplies | NotAllowed | ReopenWindowPassed
    if actor.IsCustomer():
        customerReplies(ticket, internal)
    #> An agent's answer ends the customer's wait -> tickets.Service.agentReplies | TicketClosed
    elif not internal:
        agentReplies(ticket, actor)
    # an agent's internal note skips both, even when closed
    #> Add the reply
    add Reply(body, internal, by actor)
    #> Tell the people concerned -> tickets.Service.announceReply
    announceReply(ticket, by=actor, internal)
    return visibleTo(actor, ticket)

=== tickets.Service.customerReplies
kind: def
src: internal/tickets/tickets.go :: func (s *Service) customerReplies(
doc: What a customer's reply does to the ticket. A ticket waiting on them comes back to us. A closed ticket reopens, but only within seven days of closing.
---
def customerReplies(ticket, internal):
    #> Customers cannot write internal notes | NotAllowed
    if internal:
        raise NotAllowed
    #> A closed ticket reopens within 7 days -> tickets.Service.move | ReopenWindowPassed
    if ticket.Status == "closed":
        if now - ticket.ClosedAt > 7 days:
            raise ReopenWindowPassed
        move(ticket, "open")   # a new deadline starts
    #> A ticket waiting on them comes back to us -> tickets.Service.move
    elif ticket.Status == "waiting":
        move(ticket, "open")   # a new deadline starts
    # "new" or "open": no change, the deadline keeps running

=== tickets.Service.agentReplies
kind: def
src: internal/tickets/tickets.go :: func (s *Service) agentReplies(
doc: What an agent's answer does to the ticket: the customer's wait ends, and an agent who answers a ticket nobody has takes it.
---
def agentReplies(ticket, actor):
    #> A closed ticket must be reopened first | TicketClosed
    if ticket.Status == "closed":
        raise TicketClosed
    #> Answering a ticket nobody has takes it
    if ticket.AssignedAgentID is empty:
        ticket.AssignedAgentID = actor.AgentID
    #> Now we wait for the customer -> tickets.Service.move
    if ticket.Status != "waiting":
        move(ticket, "waiting")   # the deadline stops

=== tickets.Service.ChangePriority
kind: def
src: internal/tickets/tickets.go :: func (s *Service) ChangePriority(
doc: Sets how urgent a ticket is and works its deadline out again. Setting the priority it already has does nothing.
---
def ChangePriority(actor, id, text):
    #> Find a ticket they may see -> tickets.Service.find | TicketNotFound
    ticket = find(actor, id)
    #> Only agents on its team -> tickets.CanWorkOn | NotAllowed
    if not CanWorkOn(actor, ticket):
        raise NotAllowed
    #> Not on a closed ticket | TicketClosed
    if ticket.Status == "closed":
        raise TicketClosed
    #> Read the priority -> deadlines.ParsePriority | UnknownPriority
    priority = ParsePriority(text)
    if priority == ticket.Priority:
        return ticket   # nothing to do, nobody is told
    #> Set it and move the deadline -> tickets.Service.retime
    ticket.Priority = priority
    retime(ticket)
    #> Tell whoever has the ticket -> tickets.Service.announcePriority
    announcePriority(ticket, by=actor)
    return visibleTo(actor, ticket)

=== tickets.Service.Close
kind: def
src: internal/tickets/tickets.go :: func (s *Service) Close(
doc: Ends a ticket. Anyone who may see it may close it: its customer, or an agent on its team.
---
def Close(actor, id):
    #> Find a ticket they may see -> tickets.Service.find | TicketNotFound
    ticket = find(actor, id)
    #> Close it, which ends the deadline -> tickets.Service.move | StatusChange
    move(ticket, "closed")   # closed twice: refused
    #> Tell the other side -> tickets.Service.announceClosed
    announceClosed(ticket, by=actor)
    return visibleTo(actor, ticket)

=== tickets.Service.Reopen
kind: def
src: internal/tickets/tickets.go :: func (s *Service) Reopen(
doc: Brings a closed ticket back to the team and starts a new deadline.
---
def Reopen(actor, id):
    #> Find a ticket they may see -> tickets.Service.find | TicketNotFound
    ticket = find(actor, id)
    #> Only a closed ticket reopens | StatusChange
    if ticket.Status != "closed":
        raise StatusChange
    #> Within 7 days, unless a lead -> tickets.CanReopen | ReopenWindowPassed
    if not CanReopen(actor, ticket):
        raise ReopenWindowPassed
    #> Open it, which starts a new deadline -> tickets.Service.move
    move(ticket, "open")
    #> Tell the other side -> tickets.Service.announceReopened
    announceReopened(ticket, by=actor)
    return visibleTo(actor, ticket)

=== tickets.canMove
kind: def
src: internal/tickets/status.go :: func canMove(
doc: The status changes a ticket may make. Nothing goes back to new, and a closed ticket can only be opened again.
---
def canMove(from, to):
    allowed = {
        "new":     ["open", "waiting", "closed"]
        "open":    ["waiting", "closed"]
        "waiting": ["open", "closed"]
        "closed":  ["open"]
    }
    return to in allowed[from]

=== tickets.Service.move
kind: def
src: internal/tickets/status.go :: func (s *Service) move(
doc: Changes a ticket's status and keeps its deadline in step. The customer's wait ends when we answer or the ticket closes, and starts again when a waiting or closed ticket comes back to us.
---
def move(ticket, to):
    #> Check the change is allowed -> tickets.canMove | StatusChange
    if not canMove(ticket.Status, to):
        raise StatusChange
    from = ticket.Status
    ticket.Status = to
    #> We answered: nothing is due -> tickets.stopClock
    if to == "waiting":
        stopClock(ticket)
    #> Closed: nothing is due -> tickets.stopClock
    if to == "closed":
        stopClock(ticket)
        ticket.ClosedAt = now
    #> Back with us: a new deadline starts -> tickets.Service.startClock
    if to == "open" and from != "new":
        ticket.ClosedAt = None
        startClock(ticket)
    # "new" to "open": the first deadline keeps running

=== tickets.Service.Assign
kind: def
src: internal/tickets/assignment.go :: func (s *Service) Assign(
doc: Gives a ticket to an agent on its team. A new ticket becomes open when someone gets it; its deadline does not change.
---
def Assign(actor, id, toAgentID=None):
    #> Find a ticket they may see -> tickets.Service.find | TicketNotFound
    ticket = find(actor, id)
    #> No agent named means the caller
    toAgentID = toAgentID or actor.AgentID
    #> Check they may assign it -> tickets.CanAssign | NotAllowed
    if not CanAssign(actor, ticket, toAgentID):
        raise NotAllowed
    #> Not on a closed ticket | TicketClosed
    if ticket.Status == "closed":
        raise TicketClosed
    #> The agent must be active and on the team -> accounts.Directory.Agent | AssigneeNotInTeam
    assignee = accounts.Directory.Agent(toAgentID)
    if none, or not assignee.Active,
            or assignee.TeamID != ticket.TeamID:
        raise AssigneeNotInTeam
    if ticket.AssignedAgentID == toAgentID:
        return ticket   # already theirs, nobody is told
    #> Hand it over
    previous = ticket.AssignedAgentID
    ticket.AssignedAgentID = toAgentID
    #> A new ticket becomes open -> tickets.Service.move
    if ticket.Status == "new":
        move(ticket, "open")
    #> Tell the new and the previous agent -> tickets.Service.announceAssigned
    announceAssigned(ticket, previous, by=actor)
    return visibleTo(actor, ticket)

=== tickets.Service.Escalate
kind: def
src: internal/tickets/escalation.go :: func (s *Service) Escalate(
doc: A lead says a ticket needs more attention. A ticket is escalated once; the reason, if given, is kept as an internal note.
---
def Escalate(actor, id, reason=None):
    #> Find a ticket they may see -> tickets.Service.find | TicketNotFound
    ticket = find(actor, id)
    #> Only a lead of its team -> tickets.CanEscalate | NotAllowed
    if not CanEscalate(actor, ticket):
        raise NotAllowed
    #> Not closed, and not escalated before | TicketClosed | AlreadyEscalated
    if ticket.Status == "closed":
        raise TicketClosed
    if ticket.Escalated:
        raise AlreadyEscalated
    #> Raise the priority, bring the deadline closer -> tickets.Service.escalate
    escalate(ticket)
    #> Keep the reason as an internal note
    if reason:
        add Reply("Escalated: " + reason, Internal, by actor)
    #> Tell the assignee and the customer -> tickets.Service.announceEscalated
    announceEscalated(ticket, by=actor)
    return visibleTo(actor, ticket)

=== tickets.Service.escalate
kind: def
src: internal/tickets/escalation.go :: func (s *Service) escalate(
doc: Marks a ticket escalated and raises its priority one step, which brings its deadline closer. Used when a lead escalates and when a ticket passes its deadline.
---
def escalate(ticket):
    ticket.Escalated = True
    #> One step more urgent -> deadlines.Priority.Raised
    ticket.Priority = ticket.Priority.Raised()
    #> Work the deadline out again -> tickets.Service.retime
    retime(ticket)

=== Opening a ticket
kind: flow
domain: Tickets
doc: What happens between a customer asking for help and a team knowing about it.
---
#> The customer writes in -> POST /tickets
A signed-in customer sends a subject, a message, a topic and how urgent it is.
An agent can open a ticket for a customer they name.
#> The request is checked -> tickets.Service.Open
A subject and a message are needed. A customer on the free plan may ask for high priority at most; other plans may ask for urgent. Agents may set any priority.
#> A team gets the ticket -> accounts.Directory.TeamForTopic
The topic decides which team handles it. A topic no team lists goes to the catch-all team.
#> The deadline starts -> tickets.Service.startClock
The ticket is new, with the message as its first reply. From this moment a reply is due within the time the priority and the customer's plan allow.
#> The team hears about it -> tickets.Service.announceOpened
The team's leads get a notice. If an agent opened the ticket, the customer gets one too.

=== Answering a ticket
kind: flow
domain: Tickets
doc: How a ticket goes back and forth between the team and the customer until it is closed.
---
#> An agent takes the ticket -> POST /tickets/{id}/assign
An agent on the team takes a ticket nobody has, or a lead gives it to someone. A new ticket becomes open. The deadline keeps running.
#> The agent answers -> POST /tickets/{id}/replies
The answer ends the customer's wait: the ticket is now waiting and has no deadline. An agent who answers a ticket nobody has takes it. The customer gets a notice.
#> Agents leave notes for each other -> tickets.Service.Reply
An internal note is seen by agents only and changes nothing about the ticket.
#> The customer writes back -> tickets.Service.customerReplies
The ticket is open again and a new deadline starts from that moment. Whoever has the ticket gets a notice.
#> Someone closes it -> POST /tickets/{id}/close
The customer or an agent on the team closes the ticket. Nothing is due any more, and the other side is told.

=== A customer replies to a closed ticket
kind: flow
domain: Tickets
doc: What a late reply does, depending on how long ago the ticket closed.
---
#> The customer sends a reply -> POST /tickets/{id}/replies
The customer writes on one of their own tickets that has been closed.
#> Within seven days, the ticket reopens -> tickets.Service.customerReplies
The ticket is open again, with the same assignee, and a new deadline starts.
After seven days the reply is refused and the customer is asked to open a new ticket.
#> The team is told -> tickets.Service.announceReply
The assignee gets a notice of the new reply, or the team's leads if nobody has the ticket.
#> A lead can still reopen an old ticket -> POST /tickets/{id}/reopen
Reopening by hand follows the same seven days for customers and agents. A lead of the team may reopen at any time.

=== Escalating a ticket
kind: flow
domain: Tickets
doc: A lead decides a ticket needs more attention than it is getting.
---
#> A lead escalates -> POST /tickets/{id}/escalate
Only a lead of the ticket's team may, on a ticket that is not closed and has not been escalated before. They can give a reason.
#> The ticket becomes more urgent -> tickets.Service.escalate
Its priority goes up one step; urgent stays urgent. If the customer is waiting, the deadline is worked out again from when their wait began, so it comes closer.
#> The reason is kept -> tickets.Service.Escalate
The reason is saved on the ticket as an internal note, which the customer does not see.
#> People are told -> tickets.Service.announceEscalated
The assignee gets a notice, and the customer is told their ticket is getting extra attention.
